  "proof_explanation": "On entry from JSR/BSR caller, [A7] holds the immediate caller return PC and [A7+4] holds the grandparent return PC. Executing ADDQ.L #4, A7 at 0x00E6A6 pops the immediate caller return frame (+4 bytes), and RTS at 0x00E6A8 pops the grandparent return PC (+4 bytes, total A7 delta = +8 bytes), aborting the active sub-action directly back to the grandparent dispatcher.",
